r.com/2026/07/18/what-weve-learned-about-yaxel-lendeborg-from-warriors-summer-league/))

The 6-foot-9, 241-pound forward arrived after six college seasons, including time at UAB following a community college stint, and was selected by Golden State in the 2026 NBA Draft. ([chicoer.com](https://www.chicoer.com/2026/07/18/what-weve-learned-about-yaxel-lendeborg-from-warriors-summer-league/)) His earlier collegiate seasons had generated a non-shooter label that trailed him into draft projections, but his statistics shifted substantially over his final three years â€” Bay Area News Group reporter Shae Hammond notes a 37 percent mark from three-point range across that span. ([chicoer.com](https://www.chicoer.com/2026/07/18/what-weve-learned-about-yaxel-lendeborg-from-warriors-summer-league/))

## The Shooting Question

Summer League has offered early evidence on the same question. At the California Classic â€” played before the Las Vegas portion of the schedule â€” Lendeborg connected on 7 of 9 three-point attempts across two games, a pace the Bay Area News Group described as scorching and backed by sound underlying numbers. ([chicoer.com](https://www.chicoer.com/2026/07/18/what-weve-learned-about-yaxel-lendeborg-from-warriors-summer-league/)) Across the broader Summer League sample, he had made 15 of 31 three-point attempts â€” a small count by design, but the outlet characterized it as a striking rate. ([chicoer.com](https://www.chicoer.com/2026/07/18/what-weve-learned-about-yaxel-lendeborg-from-warriors-summer-league/))

Early returns indicate his shooting presents a credible threat, per the Bay Area News Group. ([chicoer.com](https://www.chicoer.com/2026/07/18/what-weve-learned-about-yaxel-lendeborg-from-warriors-summer-league/)) His mechanics are described as compact, with most attempts coming from the corners in catch-and-shoot situations â€” the profile of a wing specialist rather than a shot creator. The outlet connected him to comparisons with De'Anthony Melton in terms of the specific function he would be expected to fill, noting that reporters had asked him about playing alongside Steph Curry. ([chicoer.com](https://www.chicoer.com/2026/07/18/what-weve-learned-about-yaxel-lendeborg-from-warriors-summer-league/))

## On-Court Numbers

Individual game contributions have reinforced the multi-dimensional reading. In one contest, Lendeborg put up 15 points, four rebounds, three assists, and two blocks. ([chicoer.com](https://www.chicoer.com/2026/07/18/what-weve-learned-about-yaxel-lendeborg-from-warriors-summer-league/)) In another, he scored 16 points, with other players rotating through supporting roles. ([chicoer.com](https://www.chicoer.com/2026/07/18/what-weve-learned-about-yaxel-lendeborg-from-warriors-summer-league/))

The Warriors entered the tournament's later rounds with momentum behind them: they topped Memphis 106-85 in their opening game on Tuesday and then defeated the Los Angeles Lakers 92-88 to advance to the Summer League playoff semifinals, going 3-1 through the Las Vegas competition. ([chicoer.com](https://www.chicoer.com/2026/07/18/what-weve-learned-about-yaxel-lendeborg-from-warriors-summer-league/))

## A Roster Context Worth Watching

The more pressing question is whether Lendeborg's Summer League form translates into minutes when the regular season opens. The Bay Area News Group's reporting places him in a 2026-27 rotation context shaped by injury absences: Jimmy Butler and Moses Moody â€” the latter dealing with a knee issue â€” are both expected to miss time, and Lendeborg is among those projected to handle a significant share of minutes in Steve Kerr's rotation. ([chicoer.com](https://www.chicoer.com/2026/07/18/what-weve-learned-about-yaxel-lendeborg-from-warriors-summer-league/)) The outlet is careful to note that Summer League performance remains an imperfect indicator of readiness for the main roster. ([chicoer.com](https://www.chicoer.com/2026/07/18/what-weve-learned-about-yaxel-lendeborg-from-warriors-summer-league/))

